    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d100">

                <pb facs="0364" n="78" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg78"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Droppers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-04T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 4, 1916, 2 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>154. Your 189, December 2. Navy Department and this Department agree inadvisable
                    send <hi rendition="#italic">Des Moines</hi> to Athens. Are you in imminent
                    danger?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For a description of the situation in Germany with respect to food supply,
                        etc., see despatch No. 4530, November 7, received December 4, from the
                        Chargé in Germany, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg314"
                            >page 314</ref>.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
